# A list grown inside a loop's beat keeps its storage outside the arena, and
# the beat that would reclaim the list's header frees that storage when it
# rewinds (#2015). Here `fill` carries a bag record through its beat and
# `laps` is the beat around it. Before the fix, the pop of `fill`'s beat
# walked the bag to repair it and copied the list's items into the arena,
# leaving the outside buffer with nothing pointing at it, so one 8,208-byte
# buffer was still live at exit. The pop now repairs only the slots, and
# perm_live_bytes reads zero.
type bag
  count
  items

fn add b i
  bag (b.count + 1) (push b.items i)

fn fill b 0
  b

fn fill b n
  fill (add b n) (n - 1)

fn total n
  length (fill (bag 0 []) n).items

fn laps acc 0
  acc

fn laps acc n
  laps (acc + total 300) (n - 1)

pub play = print (laps 0 4)
